   "text": {
    "L1": "Directions are fixed on the ground: north, south, east and west.",
    "L2": "North is often drawn at the top of a map, but north is not always up in real life.",
    "L3": "On a map, east is right and west is left when north is at the top.",
    "L4": "Left and right depend on which way you face. If you face north and turn right, you face east.",
    "L5": "The sun rises in the east. Facing the morning sun, north is on your left and west is behind you.",
    "L6": "Good directions name the turn, how far to go, and a landmark to check your route.",
    "L7": "Ammu goes north, turns right, then turns right again. Which way does she face?",
    "L8": "She faces east after the first turn, then south after the second turn."
   },
